All three new stories use `startOpen: true` to expose the open state for visual testing, but per project conventions interactive component stories should use a `play` function to programmatically trigger the interaction. This ensures the open/expanded state is captured in visual regression tests and makes the test intent explicit. For example:

```tsx
play: async ({ canvasElement }) => {
  const canvas = within(canvasElement);
  await userEvent.click(canvas.getByRole('button', { name: /color/i }));
},
```
